          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-[#1A1F22] mb-4">Inherited & Estate Safe Opening</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            One of the most common safe lockout scenarios is an inherited safe â€” a family member or estate has left behind a safe, and the combination was never documented or has been lost. These situations are handled with sensitivity and care, and we may request documentation of inheritance or estate administration before opening.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-3">
            The approach depends entirely on the safe model. Older mechanical combination safes can often be opened via dial manipulation. Older electronic safes may have accessible override codes. Some older safes have simple key locks that can be picked or bypassed. We assess each situation individually.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
